# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# clk -> wclk: the tunnel's clock crossing (lvds-tunnel.md §4.8), cut.
#
# Here and not in impl_1.sdc: wclk is not created by us. Radiant derives
# it after synthesis from ECLKDIV (create_generated_clock -name {wclk}
# ... -divide_by 4, see the .twr section 1.1), so a get_clocks wclk in the
# .sdc is dropped at synthesis ("No clock matched"; the companion's .srp
# shows exactly that for its own wclk).
#
# wclk is clk/4 from the same PLL, so STA would time clk -> wclk as a
# synchronous path. The RTL does not rely on it: everything that crosses
# (capture_buffer: rbank, frame_index, alt_cmd, alt_answer; tun_aux:
# flags_snap, send_config, send_status, shadow_snap via cfg_byte) is
# written once per sampling period, at the announcement, and read by
# frame_builder only after frame_rdy has passed its 2-flop synchroniser,
# >= 1 wclk (~105 ns at 25 kSPS) later; it is then stable for the rest of
# the period. frame_rdy is the synchroniser's input. wbank (EBR) is
# written on clk and read on wclk, never the same bank at once.
#
# One direction only. wclk -> clk stays timed: it is not part of this
# handshake, and ODDRX4's gearing between wclk and eclk (clk through
# ECLKSYNC) is a real synchronous relationship.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
set_false_path -from [get_clocks clk] -to [get_clocks wclk]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# clk -> clk_tx: the #6a MOSI register (spi1-mosi-eye-scan.md §3.1, O2).
#
# clk_tx's phase moves at run time, so STA cannot time this crossing at
# the phase in use; by default it times it as at phase 0 (a full period
# from clk rising, T/2 from clk falling), far looser than what the scan
# relies on. The scan allows only phases where the clk_tx edge comes at
# least T/4 after the source changes, so every source (m_early,
# combinational after clk rising: regbank EBR -> txsr's load mux -> the
# source mux; m0; and the clk-falling copies) must settle within
# T/4 - 1 ns of its own launch edge.
#
# Here and not in the .sdc: the register's name only exists after
# synthesis. In the .sdc, LSE cannot resolve it (13 warnings) and map
# then times it from its own copy; here the RTL name (get_cells
# scan0/mosi_tx) and the cell name (scan0/mosi_tx_c) are both dropped by
# map with only a map warning, which looks like a clean build. Only the
# pin form below is applied: check for its "Path Exception" in the .twr
# (build_kuntur.py does) after any change that could rename it.
#
# One .pdc for all three builds, so one value: T/4 - 1 at 28k
# (23.527 ns -> 4.881 ns). At 25k it is 5.587 ns; 4.881 is 0.71 ns
# tighter than needed there.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
set_max_delay -from [get_clocks clk] -to [get_pins {scan0/mosi_tx_c.ff_inst/DF}] 4.881
